# A tripwire, not a workaround. The DeepSeek runtime lives inside WSL, so every
# host path handed to it goes through runtimePath() (deepseek/process-manager.ts)
# first. A Windows path that skips that seam is read as a RELATIVE Linux name and
# the runtime creates one directory literally called
#   C:\Users\...\Temp\...
# One such fossil (from a pre-rename live sandbox run) sat here and was removed
# on 2026-08-24. Turn cwd and tool paths are both mapped today, so this pattern
# should never match again — it stays because the live sandbox test needs a real
# key plus WSL and therefore never runs in CI.
C*Users*AppData*Local*Temp*/

